  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 隻\ntitle: ship counter; one of a pair\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 隹\nradicalNumber: 172\nonyomi: [セキ]\nkunyomi: []\ndistractors: [集, 進, 受]\n---\n\n# 隻 — ship counter; one of a pair\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 隹 (no. 172) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n隻 is used to count ships and can refer to one half of a pair. 一隻 counts one ship; the character is not the ordinary noun for a boat.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See a 隹-shaped bird above a 又-shaped hand holding just one item. This is a modern-shape memory aid, not a historical account.\n\nThe canonical radical is 隹, no. 172, in the upper part.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| セキ | on | 一隻 いっせき - one ship; 隻 supplies セキ |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [隻](../words/隻.md) せき - counter for ships\n- 一隻 いっせき - one ship; one boat\n\n## Notes\n\n- In 一隻 いっせき, the 一 part takes いっ before セキ. Learn the whole numeral-counter form rather than pronouncing it いちせき.\n- JMdict also records a counter for half of a pair, such as half of a folding screen. Its bundle-item counter for fish, birds or arrows is marked archaic; that does not make the ship-counter sense archaic.\n- Compare [集](集.md), gather, which also contains 隹 but has a different lower part and whole-character meaning.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1164100, 2038290.\n",
